DELF A2 Part 3 for an English-speaking candidate: a role-play card whose first instruction, with "vous", states an everyday situation in France (buying, booking or inviting), with the points to sort out as prompts. The examiner plays the other person with the facts it knows (prices in euros, times, conditions) realistic for France, reacts to what the candidate asks and uses greetings and polite forms. The role names that person in English, and the summary is in English.